formatted_question:
 S Select the best translation into predicate logic. Some kind people help some endangered species. (Ex: x is endangered; Kx: x is kind; Px: x is a person; Sx: x is a species; Hxy: x helps y)
(A) (∃x)(∃y){[(Kx • Px) • (Ey • Sy)] ⊃ Hxy}
(B) (∃x){(Kx • Px) • (∃y)[(Ey • Sy) • Hxy]}

counterfactual_question_0:
Translate the sentence "Some kind people help every endangered species." into predicate logic. (Ex: x is endangered; Kx: x is kind; Px: x is a person; Sx: x is a species; Hxy: x helps y)
(A) (∃x)(∀y){[(Kx • Px) • (Ey • Sy)] ⊃ Hxy}
(B) (∃x){(Kx • Px) • (∀y)[(Ey • Sy) ⊃ Hxy]}

